Real, verified unified diff (git diff in target/gecko-src/gecko-dev,
branch central-work @ 5836a062726f715fda621338a17b51aff30d0a8c) against
the upstream file browser/components/nsIBrowserHandler.idl — apply with
`git apply` or `patch -p1` from the checkout root.

Adds a read-only pyxisAppId attribute to nsIBrowserHandler, mirroring
the existing `kiosk` attribute on the same interface, so
BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs's new gPyxisAppId state (see
BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs.PYXIS_DIFF in the sibling directory) is
reachable off Cc["@mozilla.org/browser/clh;1"].getService(Ci.nsIBrowserHandler)
the same way BrowserHandler.kiosk already is.

UPDATE (2026-07-06): the comment below now references `--pyxis-app`, not
the original `--app` — see BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs.PYXIS_DIFF's
dated correction note for why (a real collision with Gecko's own native
`-app <path>` startup flag, found via a real failed boot).

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/browser/components/nsIBrowserHandler.idl b/browser/components/nsIBrowserHandler.idl
index 8666f79e57e8..d9f0b01e4bb7 100644
--- a/browser/components/nsIBrowserHandler.idl
+++ b/browser/components/nsIBrowserHandler.idl
@@ -16,6 +16,21 @@ interface nsIBrowserHandler : nsISupports
   attribute boolean majorUpgrade;
   attribute boolean firstRunProfile;
 
+  /**
+   * PYXIS: the app id passed via `--pyxis-app=<id>`/PYXIS_APP_ID, or an
+   * empty string for a normal (non-pyxis-webapp) browser launch. Read-only
+   * from script; nsBrowserContentHandler sets its backing gPyxisAppId value
+   * internally when it recognizes `--pyxis-app` in bch_handle (see
+   * BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs -- note the flag is `--pyxis-app`, NOT
+   * plain `--app`, which collides with a pre-existing native Gecko flag of
+   * the same name used for an unrelated alternate-application.ini feature;
+   * see BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs's dated correction comment for the
+   * real failure this caused). Mirrors the existing `kiosk` attribute
+   * above, which is the real precedent for exposing command-line-derived
+   * launch-mode state through this interface.
+   */
+  readonly attribute AUTF8String pyxisAppId;
+
   /**
    * Extract the width and height specified on the command line, if present.
    * @return A feature string with a prepended comma, e.g. ",width=500,height=400"
